                    "title": "Toward an Integrated Machine Learning Model of a ...",
                    "content": "We brought together proteomics data generators, repository managers, and machine learning experts in a workshop with the goals to evaluate and explore machine learning applications for realistic modeling of data from multidimensional mass spectrometry-based proteomics analysis of any sample or organism. Although machine learning has been applied to individual phases of a proteomics experiment, efforts in combining these into one model have been limited, and there is no comprehensive model that can predict the data for any given sample type, sample preparation, or analysis method required for quality assessment, experimental optimization, or algorithm development. This was accomplished by bringing together researchers who apply machine learning to individual steps of proteomics experiments, such as enzymatic digestion, chromatography, ion mobility, and tandem mass spectrometry, with experts on data repositories and open data formats, as well as practitioners of proteomics representing the end users of machine learned models.",
